WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.760
We ask a lot of questions
about our diet.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.080
What’s the right way to
treat a chronic illness?

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.720
Fight off a virus,
lose weight?

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.640
The problem is, we get
a lot of different answers.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.920
Well, I’m here to help.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.400
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.720
The new class
of weight-loss drugs,

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.040
GLP-1 agonists like Ozempic,

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.600
have received enormous,
almost unprecedented, attention

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.400
in the mainstream media.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.600
They’ve been called "the medical
sensation of the decade."

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.640
The business press
was practically giddy,

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.120
declaring the end
of the obesity epidemic.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.960
The enthusiasm is shared
in the medical literature,

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.040
with headlines suggesting

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.600
they are game-changing
revolutions

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.280
in the treatment of obesity:

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.960
therapeutic-wizard miracle drugs

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.520
that are hugely effective
in the treatment of obesity.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:01.400
But history is littered with
failed weight-loss wonder drugs.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.960
Every other year or so,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.680
an anti-obesity medication
that had been approved

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.120
to be safe and effective

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.400
has had to be withdrawn
from the market

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.026
after serious side effects
emerged.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.840
To date, most weight-loss drugs,
despite their initial approval,

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.840
have since been
pulled from the market

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.600
for unforeseen side effects

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.200
that have turned them
into a public threat.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.680
From "rainbow diet pills"
packed with amphetamines

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.920
that were marketed to women,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.200
to the rise and fall of fen-phen

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.120
(which triggered catastrophic
heart and lung conditions),

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.600
history is beset
by failures to find

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.440
safe, successful
weight-loss drugs.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.800
Aminorex was a widely prescribed
appetite suppressant

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.360
before it was pulled
for causing lung damage.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.960
Eighteen million Americans
were on fen-phen

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.200
before it was pulled for causing
severe damage to heart valves.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.200
Meridia was pulled
for heart attacks and strokes,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.000
and Acomplia for psychiatric
side effects, including suicide.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.360
Belviq was withdrawn in 2020

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.880
after it was recognized that
it may have been causing cancer

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.360
for the eight years
it had been on the market.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.000
The U.S. Food and Drug
Administration

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.880
initially rejected it
after it appeared to cause

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.600
several types of tumors in rats,

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:14.160
but when a one-year human trial
showed no apparent cancer,

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.520
it was approved
and went on to become

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.600
one of the most frequently
prescribed weight-loss drugs.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.680
But when people were actually
on it for a few years,

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.760
notably high rates of colorectal
cancer, pancreatic cancer,

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.120
and lung cancer popped up;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.840
so, oopsey,
it was pulled from the market.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.240
The news was met
with surprise and confusion

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.360
among obesity medicine
specialists,

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.920
who had been
prescribing the drug

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.560
to help patients
achieve and sustain

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.600
the health benefits
of weight loss.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.760
It was particularly jarring,

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.680
because the drug was generally
regarded as being so safe,

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.760
until it wasn’t.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.760
Or take Benfluorex,
like Ozempic,

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.160
another diabetes drug repurposed
as an appetite suppressant.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.600
It caused hundreds of deaths,

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.920
but didn’t get pulled
for 33 years.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:05.040
The drug company knew about
the risks, but covered them up.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.680
Judges concluded
that the drug company’s priority

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.720
was systematically given to

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.360
"preserving
its own economic interests

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:15.440
over the safety
of the drug’s consumers."

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.080
So, historically,
anti-obesity drugs have been

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.800
kind of like cigarettes.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.000
Like smoking,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.280
popping these pills
can cause you to lose weight,

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.160
but at what cost?

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.480
The goal of weight loss is not
to fit into a skinnier casket.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.200
But they don’t even work
very well.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:36.120
The current crop of
approved meds includes Qsymia,

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:39.120
a combination of phentermine,
the phen in fen-phen,

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.720
and topiramate, a drug
that can cause seizures

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.960
if you abruptly stop taking it.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.800
This drug combination
was explicitly rejected

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.120
multiple times
for safety reasons in Europe

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.240
but remains for sale
in the United States.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.680
Contrave is another option,

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:56.000
if you choose to ignore
its own black-box warning

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.680
about a potential increase
in suicidal thoughts.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:02.360
Alli, also sold as Xenical,
is the final choice.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.880
That’s the drug
that blocks fat absorption

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:09.440
and causes side effects such
as "flatus with discharge."

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:12.400
The drug evidently "forces
the patient to use diapers

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.360
and to know the location

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.760
of all the bathrooms
in the neighborhood

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.240
in an attempt
to limit the consequences

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:20.200
of urgent leakage
of oily fecal matter."

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.160
All for a grand total
of just 3 percent weight loss.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.240
All that mess to go from, like,
300 pounds (135 kg)

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.885
down to 291 pounds (130 kg).

00:04:29.885 --> 00:04:31.680
As you can see,
older weight-loss medications

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.640
only achieved about
5 percent weight loss,

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.280
whereas the newfangled
GLP-1 agonists like Ozempic

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:39.720
can cause an average of...

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.360
6 percent weight loss!

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.560
Now, this is because they were
averaging the effects

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:49.240
of some of the older GLP-1
agonists like Saxenda or Byetta.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:52.160
Semaglutide,
sold as Ozempic for diabetes

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.240
and Wegovy for weight loss,

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.240
causes about twice that.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.880
And now, there’s tirzepatide,
sold as Mounjaro or Zepbound,

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:05.000
which gets you closer to what
you see with bariatric surgery.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.400
So, while the older
obesity medications achieve

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.000
weight losses in
the 5 to 10 percent range,

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.600
the new generation of agents

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:14.120
are more in
the 15 to 20 percent range,

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.560
about triple what we saw
in many of the older drugs.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.960
So, for about half a century,

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.720
there’s been healthy skepticism

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.440
about new-kid-on-the-block
obesity drugs

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.000
promising profound weight loss,

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.680
only to see one after another
fail and flop,

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:32.760
but today, this historical
narrative could be in flux.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.960
Even over just
the last decade or so,

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.400
obesity rates have
spiraled out of control.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.440
Are GLP-1 receptor activators
the long-sought-after panacea

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.080
for obesity?

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:47.440
Well, first of all,
what is GLP-1?

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.600
The gastrointestinal tract
is known

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:53.680
as the largest hormone-secreting
gland in the human body,

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.640
releasing more than 20
peptide hormones.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.920
About 1 out of every 100 cells

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:03.280
lining our entire digestive
tract acts as a nutrient sensor

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:05.480
and can secrete hormones
accordingly,

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:10.000
including GLP-1,
glucagon-like peptide-1.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.320
The primary stimuli
for GLP-1 secretion

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.720
are meals rich in fats
and carbohydrates,

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:20.680
and the main action of GLP-1 is
to signal nutritional abundance

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.600
to the brain,
reducing our appetite

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.120
so we don’t eat
too many doughnuts.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:29.240
GLP-1 also slows things down,
allowing us more time to digest,

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:32.120
and the slowing of the rate
at which food leaves our stomach

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.040
helps with blood sugar control
after a meal.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.240
So, GLP-1 hormone-mimicking
drugs were actually

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:41.720
first developed to treat
type 2 diabetes.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:44.520
The reason you can’t just
give people GLP-1 directly

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.800
is because it’s broken down
so quickly,

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.480
it hardly even makes it
one time around the circulation,

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:54.920
thanks to inactivation
by an enzyme in our body.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:57.280
But then,
a compound was discovered

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:59.600
that activates GLP-1 activity

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.240
but was resistant
to enzyme breakdown.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:05.320
And it was found in a lizard.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:08.800
It’s a constituent
of Gila Monster venom.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.800
And the first drug was born.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:11.920
Using that as a template,

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:13.920
the first GLP-1 agonist
was created

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.840
and approved
for the treatment of diabetes

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:17.840
about 20 years ago.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.760
Instead of half lasting
2.5 minutes in the body,

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:23.120
it lasted about 2.5 hours,

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.720
but still had to be injected
twice a day.

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:28.880
Then came liraglutide,
which lasts all day,

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:32.040
but even once-a-day injections
can be a pain.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:35.960
Enter semaglutide,
branded as Ozempic,

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:38.880
which could be injected
just once a week.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:41.440
It was approved to treat
diabetes in 2017.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.800
Within a few years, a daily oral
version had been developed,

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.440
again for diabetes,

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.560
but researchers running
those clinical trials

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.840
noticed a surprising
side effect:

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:53.040
people’s appetites diminished.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:56.640
Indeed, if you drip the hormone
GLP-1 into people’s veins,

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.240
it reduces their appetite,

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:00.520
leading
to decreased food intake.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:02.080
And not just a little.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.800
We’re talking about
a decrease in caloric intake

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:07.760
by as much as 25 to 50 percent.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:11.160
The GLP-1 hormone not only
slows stomach emptying--

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:14.320
so you feel fuller longer
after eating--

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.400
but also works
as an appetite suppressant

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.720
by triggering
parts of the brain

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.240
responsible
for hunger and cravings.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:24.440
GLP-1-secreting cells don’t
only line our intestines;

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.520
they’re also in our brains.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:31.400
So, GLP-1 agonist drugs,
meaning GLP-1-mimicking drugs,

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:34.560
work kind of like
the way birth control pills do.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:38.160
Birth control pills mimic
placental hormones,

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.480
thereby tricking our body

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:41.760
into thinking we’re pregnant
all the time.

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:44.640
Ozempic-type drugs mimic GLP-1,

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:45.840
thereby tricking our body

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:48.160
into thinking
we’re eating all the time;

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.600
so, it dials down
our hunger drive.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.640
In 2021, semaglutide,

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:55.040
originally approved as Ozempic
to treat diabetes,

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.640
was rebranded at a higher dose
as Wegovy to treat obesity,

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.680
and the weight-loss industry
changed overnight,

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.880
shifting away
from meal replacements

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:07.640
and portion-control plans

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:10.080
to the new world
of private equity-funded

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.240
telemedicine entities

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:14.320
set up to offer these
injectable weight-loss drugs.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.360
Even Weight Watchers has openly
embraced these kinds of drugs

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.320
as the future of weight loss.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:22.200
They were even approved
for kids as young as age 12--

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.360
tweens, not even teens.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:25.840
Is that a good idea?

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:27.440
What are the pros and cons

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:29.840
of these new
weight-loss medications?

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.760
Older weight-loss
medications achieve

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.120
approximately 5 percent
reduction in body weight

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:35.280
over placebo,

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.080
whereas these new GLP-1
agonists, like Ozempic,

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:41.120
produce about triple the effect,
about 15 percent.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:44.280
But what does that mean in terms
of numbers on the scale?

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:47.800
In an analysis of more than
100 clinical trials

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:50.320
of earlier anti-obesity
medications,

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.840
in studies lasting
up to 76 weeks,

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:55.320
drug-induced weight loss
never exceeded

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:58.200
more than 9 pounds (4 kg).

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.120
If you put all the GLP-1 drug
trials together,

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:02.760
over an average of about a year,

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:06.680
they led to about 19 pounds
(8 kg) of weight loss.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:10.120
And that folded in
some of the older GLP-1 drugs,

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:12.480
like liraglutide,
that don’t work as well.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.200
If you just look at semaglutide,

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:17.960
the high-dose Ozempic
sold as Wegovy for weight loss,

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:21.720
we’re looking at more like
27 pounds (12 kg) lost,

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.320
which translates into about
three and a half inches (9 cm)

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.080
off the waist.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.600
Which GLP-1 drug works best?

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.440
An oral version of Ozempic
has been developed.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.640
Though it hasn’t been approved
for weight loss,

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:37.560
preliminary evidence suggests
it causes similar weight loss

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:39.520
to the injectable version.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:43.400
The latest GLP-1 drug approved
for weight loss, tirzepatide,

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.840
sold as Zepbound,
appears to beat out semaglutide,

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:49.560
with nearly 19 percent
of body weight lost,

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:50.920
over 40 pounds (18 kg),

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.560
with more like five and a half
inches (14 cm) off the waist.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:57.280
How does that compare
to bariatric surgery?

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:59.040
It’s actually not that far off

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:02.000
from long-term
surgical weight loss.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.120
Now, remember,
these are averages.

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.880
Bariatric surgery
doesn’t always work.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:09.080
The failure rate
for the gold standard procedure

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:11.200
is approximately 20 percent,

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.720
but not everyone responds
to the GLP-1 drugs either.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:16.120
In the big Ozempic trials,

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:19.600
about a third of people were
"super responders,"

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:22.960
but as many as one in six didn’t
lose significant weight at all,

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:25.520
even after taking the drug
for more than a year.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:28.560
So, despite impressive results
at a population level,

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.280
up to 20 percent of patients

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:32.080
fail to achieve
significant weight loss

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:35.360
with either surgical
or drug-based approaches.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:37.400
Here’s the longest trial
to date,

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:41.840
four years of high-dose Ozempic
for weight loss at the end of Year Two.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.360
The average weight loss was
about 10 percent;

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:47.080
so, some lost even more weight,

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.200
and sometimes,
a lot more weight,

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.160
some lost less,

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.120
and some even gained weight,

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.640
as much as maybe 40 pounds
(18 kg),

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:58.137
even after continuing
to inject the drug for years.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:02.760
OK, but the most striking thing
about this graph is the plateau.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:05.840
They were being injected with
the drug the whole four years,

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:09.120
but weight loss stalled
after only about a year.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.360
This happened in study after
study after study after study,

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.240
with both Ozempic
and the newer tirzepatide.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.920
So, even under
the best of circumstances,

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.120
with the most potent GLP-1 drugs

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:22.760
taken at the highest
allowable dose

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.720
for at least a year
to obtain the full weight loss,

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.520
we’re only looking at
a 34-pound (15 kg) drop

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:30.840
before the weight loss stops.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:32.560
So, if you look at all three

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.040
of the original
placebo-controlled

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.920
Ozempic weight loss trials,

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.680
the participants
started out obese,

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:40.720
and after more than a year
on the drug

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:42.760
(when it effectively
stopped working),

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:45.440
they were still obese.

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:49.000
They were certainly less obese,
but still obese.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:52.040
Then, to keep yourself
at that same level of obese,

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.720
you still have
to keep injecting it

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:55.640
at, like, $1,000 a month,

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:59.838
or you’ll go back to your
original level of obese.

